    "representation": "Keep every recognized rune including headings, grouped by archived source line. Ignore non-rune characters and lines with no runes. Retain original line and within-line rune positions. LP2-50 is retained as a zero-rune page, with no candidate routes. Left-align rune rows by within-row ordinal. Unequal row lengths remain unequal. Missing cells are skipped, not padded. Ordinal columns are not asserted to be physical image columns.",
    "procedure": "Enumerate 16 row-first and column-first routes, both outer directions, both initial inner directions, and constant/alternating inner direction. This includes reversing the rune order within every archived row while keeping the rows in their original order, on LP2-15 and every other rune-bearing target page (row-first, forward outer direction, reversed inner direction, no alternation). Preserve every source position and compare the first 12 output indices with nine fixed known openings.",
    "parameters": "16 route configurations per nonempty page; 55 nonempty pages; 880 cases; 7920 exact opening comparisons. No substitution or later-position search.",
    "exclusions": "Arbitrary column permutations, spiral paths, rectangular reflow, physical x-coordinate alignment, heading removal, substitution, alternative openings and other text regions."
  },
  "outcome": "not-supported",
  "finding": "None of 880 routes matched any of nine known passage openings. An independent source-position check reproduced every output.",
  "limitations": "Only the first 12 runes were compared. Other beginnings, routes and columns aligned by image position remain untested.",
  "next_steps": "The fixed line-reversal plus Atbash Warning opening is already excluded by saved prefixes; see prepared-opening-evidence-gates. Physical alignment, other regions or different routes remain distinct proposals and need declared rules and evaluation criteria.",
