      "motivation": "Read each line’s runes backwards. Then replace the first alphabet rune with the last, the second with the second-last, and so on: the substitution used to decode Warning. This adds substitution to the earlier order-only check; compare the first 24 outputs with Warning’s opening.",
      "title": "Read each line backwards, then reverse the alphabet",
      "question": "Does reversing each archived line and then applying the Warning page’s Atbash mapping recover its fixed 24-rune opening?",
      "scope_change": "Adds the documented Atbash mapping to the existing line-reversal route. The prior route test excluded substitutions; the separate five-direction cipher replay did not include reversing every line.",
      "limitation": "This tests one fixed 24-rune page opening, not general readability or a complete decryption. Archived headings and separators remain included. No later starts, key skips, fitted alphabets or alternative plaintexts are searched.",
